ion_count": 37190, "like_count": 205, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 41, "retweet_count": 28}, "text": "Bloomberg re “mentions” on S&amp;P 500 corporate earnings calls:\n“…mentions of “inflation” or “inflationary” climbed to 820 on the earnings calls of S&amp;P 500 companies in October, the highest monthly figure since February 2024.”\n#economy #markets #inflation https://t.co/wG4nDYZz7D", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119204117952233795"}, {"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-11-07T22:52:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119201339020648849"], "id": "2119201339020648849", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 184, "impression_count": 46930, "like_count": 791, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 113, "retweet_count": 82}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119142310894334262", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Data scaling and compute scaling are *multipliers* for the generalization power of an approach. Trillions of dollars in investment can make very inefficient, low-generalization approaches look adequate, but that doesn't make them the ultimate end-all-be-all of AI.\n\nYou should https://t.co/kPtFXleYw1", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2119201339020648849"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-07T22:44:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119199301066694758"], "id": "2119199301066694758", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 30, "impression_count": 31463, "like_count": 187, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "In 2000 Bush won the electoral college but lost the popular vote.\n\n2004 could have been the reverse: Kerry came closer to winning the electoral college than the popular vote.\n\nIf that had happened the perception around electoral college advantages would be very different today. https://t.co/xccHcvahb8", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2119199301066694758"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-07T22:42:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119198809544630523"], "id": "2119198809544630523", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 35416, "like_count": 227, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 34, "retweet_count": 30}, "text": "While tech stock volatility grabbed most of the headlines this past week, the energy sector suffered bigger losses, as shown in this WSJ chart.\n#economy #markets #stocks #tech #energy #ArtificialIntelligence #ai @WSJ https://t.co/863JEvdGoj", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119198809544630523"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-07T22:40:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119198403620139365"], "id": "2119198403620139365", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 4539, "like_count": 94, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "You better start learning bipartisanship, buddy\n\nIf we’re gonna make it through the next few years, Ds and Rs, industry and gov’t, etc. are gonna have to work together, at the federal level at least\n\n*ducks*", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2119198403620139365"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-11-07T22:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119195692828864986"], "id": "2119195692828864986", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 24265, "like_count": 104, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 30}, "text": "How can big data and AI improve economic measurement while preserving quality, transparency, and trust? Join us at the 14th IMF Statistical Forum on November 18-19 in Washington D.C. and online. \n\nRegistration is now open.   https://t.co/D14MS64q3c https://t.co/SquyIZ3Q0s", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2119195692828864986"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-07T21:48:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119185331056718140"], "id": "2119185331056718140", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2253, "like_count": 41, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 0}, "t